    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "The most important entry this lane produced, and the one that most sharply exposes the shape of the frontier. axeyum has TWO reasoning routes with DIFFERENT logics and no object that can compare them. The SMT route fixes a two-valued Bool sort and so proves F:excluded-middle, F:double-negation-elimination and F:peirce-law in microseconds. The Lean kernel route has an intuitionistic logic prelude with zero trusted declarations, in which none of those three has a proof term and none can get one without adding an axiom. Today nothing in the stack records that a fact proved on one route is unavailable on the other, and the fact schema has no field for it: `axiom_footprint` describes the route that DID establish the fact and is silent about routes that cannot. Concretely: if a future reconstruction lane pipes an `unsat` from the SMT route into the kernel, every classical tautology in this batch is a reconstruction failure waiting to happen, and the failure will surface as a kernel error rather than as a recognised logic mismatch. That is the roadmap item. The status is `open` in the same misused sense as F:godel-first-incompleteness -- the mathematics is settled; what is open is our ability to say it.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
